# K01a witness (steps/k01-selector-identity-20261001.md §5, §5a): selector identity on an
# IDENTITY layout -- a root value whose model repeats x (no correspondence is involved).
# Bare `r\x` is the LAST occurrence, `r\[N]x` occurrence N; reads, writes and `@` resolve
# through the same occurrence-exact lookup.  Before K01a the bare read was "unresolved name"
# and `r\[0]x` lowered as C members (`l2_q2 ->[0] x`), defect
# NAMED-MODEL-OCCURRENCE-PATH-LOWERING.  Success is 7.
Tri: (size_t: x 10U; size_t: x 20U; size_t: x 30U)
fn: poke (@: size_t p) int
    \p: 77U
    return: 0
end: poke
r: merge: Tri
size_t: got 0U
int: ok 7
got: r\x
if: got != 30U
    ok: 81
got: r\[0]x
if: got != 10U
    ok: 82
got: r\[1]x
if: got != 20U
    ok: 83
got: r\[2]x
if: got != 30U
    ok: 84
r\x: 99U
got: r\x
if: got != 99U
    ok: 85
got: r\[1]x
if: got != 20U
    ok: 86
got: r\[2]x
if: got != 99U
    ok: 87
r\[0]x: 40U
got: r\[0]x
if: got != 40U
    ok: 88
got: r\x
if: got != 99U
    ok: 89
poke(@: r\[0]x)
got: r\[0]x
if: got != 77U
    ok: 90
got: r\x
if: got != 99U
    ok: 91
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
